  "goodToKnow": "Das Schiedsgericht is an arbitration tribunal that settles disputes outside the state courts, common in business and sport; the Court of Arbitration for Sport in Lausanne is the Internationaler Sportgerichtshof. Private investor-state Schiedsgerichte were a major point of protest against the TTIP trade deal around 2015. Der Schiedsrichter is a referee or arbitrator. Plural: die Schiedsgerichte."
